# Nucleus — Database & Supabase Patterns

## Table Reference
```
profiles        → user settings, plan, onboarding state
clusters        → user's workspaces (like Notion pages)
notes           → type: text | readme | canvas | chart | diagram
tasks           → with priority, due_date, cluster_id
documents       → PDFs, stored in Cloudinary, raw_text extracted
flashcards      → SM-2 spaced repetition fields
study_sessions  → timer start/end, duration_minutes
streaks         → current_streak, longest_streak, last_study_date
ai_conversations → chat metadata
ai_messages     → individual messages with role, content, attachments
```

## Query Rules

### Always filter by user_id
```ts
// CORRECT
const { data } = await supabase
  .from('notes')
  .select('id, title, type, created_at')
  .eq('user_id', user.id)
  .order('created_at', { ascending: false })

// WRONG — never do this
const { data } = await supabase.from('notes').select('*')
```

### Never use select('*') — always specify columns
```ts
// CORRECT
.select('id, title, content, cluster_id, type, updated_at')

// WRONG
.select('*')
```

### Always handle errors
```ts
const { data, error } = await supabase.from('notes').select(...)
if (error) {
  console.error('[notes] fetch error:', error.message)
  return { error: 'Failed to fetch notes' }
}
```

### cluster_id = null means "General"
```ts
// When user hasn't selected a cluster, cluster_id is null
// Never filter out null cluster_ids unless intentional
// Display null cluster_id as "General" in UI
```

## Server Actions Pattern
```ts
'use server'

import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/server'

export async function createNote(data: CreateNoteInput) {
  const supabase = await createClient()
  
  // 1. Always get user first
  const { data: { user }, error: authError } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
  if (authError || !user) return { error: 'Unauthorized' }
  
  // 2. Validate input
  if (!data.title?.trim()) return { error: 'Title is required' }
  
  // 3. Execute query with user_id
  const { data: note, error } = await supabase
    .from('notes')
    .insert({ ...data, user_id: user.id })
    .select('id, title, type')
    .single()
  
  if (error) {
    console.error('[createNote] error:', error.message)
    return { error: 'Failed to create note' }
  }
  
  return { data: note }
}
```

## API Route Auth Pattern
```ts
import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/server'
import { requirePro } from '@/lib/ai/require-pro'  // only for AI routes

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  // 1. Auth check first — always
  const supabase = await createClient()
  const { data: { user }, error } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
  if (error || !user) return new Response('Unauthorized', { status: 401 })
  
  // 2. Pro check (AI routes only)
  const proError = await requirePro(supabase)
  if (proError) return proError
  
  // 3. Parse and validate body
  const body = await req.json()
  
  // 4. Business logic
}
```

## Migrations
- All schema changes go in `supabase/migrations/` as `.sql` files
- Never modify the database directly from the Supabase dashboard for structural changes
- Migration filename format: `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql`
- Always include `IF NOT EXISTS` / `IF EXISTS` guards
- Always enable RLS on new tables: `ALTER TABLE table_name ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`
- Every new table needs at minimum: SELECT policy for owner, INSERT policy for owner

## RLS Policy Pattern (Standard Owner Policies)
```sql
-- SELECT: users can only see their own rows
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own [table]"
ON public.[table] FOR SELECT
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- INSERT: users can only insert their own rows  
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own [table]"
ON public.[table] FOR INSERT
WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- UPDATE: users can only update their own rows
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own [table]"
ON public.[table] FOR UPDATE
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- DELETE: users can only delete their own rows
CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own [table]"
ON public.[table] FOR DELETE
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

## Legacy Fields to Ignore
- `notes.subject` — legacy column, always use `cluster_id` instead
- `documents.page_count` — always null, not implemented
- `profiles.dashboard_widgets` — column exists but UI editor not built yet
